   - `Put`: if it exists, move it to the end; if new, append to the end; then if len(data) > capacity, evict order[0].

   This keeps the same structure and is O(n) per operation, which is fine for a minimal fix and matches the existing style. A more "proper" implementation would use a doubly-linked list for O(1), but the guidelines say minimal code that solves the stated problem. The existing code already uses a slice; keeping it is the surgical choice. Capacity is probably small. I'll keep the slice approach.

